/* Usage text of cfg_diff (the description of its argument parser). */
    "Compare the control flow graphs of our compiled function and the reference's, and name the structural differences.\n"
    "\n"
    "    cfg_diff <unit> <Name> [--target T|all] [--address 0x..] [--html] [--dot] [-v]\n"
    "    cfg_diff --batch [units... | --all] [--target T|all] [--select REGEX] [--all-walls] [--stopped] [--out DIR]\n"
    "\n"
    "Both sides are disassembled by recursive descent from the entry (switch tables followed through their words), cut\n"
    "into basic blocks, and the blocks of ours are aligned with the reference's: entry with entry, blocks with a unique\n"
    "call / global signature, then along the edges by role (a negated or mirrored condition crosses or keeps the arms),\n"
    "then by similarity (calls, globals, constants, opcode sequence, neighbours already mapped). What does not line up\n"
    "is named:\n"
    "\n"
    "  inverted-branch   a matched jcc pair with a negated condition and crossed arms (if/else arms swapped)\n"
    "  mirrored-compare  the same test with the cmp operands swapped (`a < b` vs `b > a`)\n"
    "  block-order       the blocks map but are laid out in another order (VC8 lays blocks out in source order)\n"
    "  duplicated-tail   the reference has a block twice that ours has once (tail duplication in the reference)\n"
    "  merged-tail       ours has a block twice that the reference has once (cross-jumped / merged there)\n"
    "  early-return      the ret/epilogue counts differ (a return from the middle vs one exit)\n"
    "  loop-rotation     one side tests a loop at the top, the other at the bottom\n"
    "  jump-threading    one side keeps a null retest (`xor r,r` arm, `test r,r`), the other threaded it\n"
    "  switch-lowering   a jump table vs a compare chain, or the cases in another order\n"
    "  tail-call         `jmp callee` on one side, `call callee` + epilogue on the other\n"
    "  missing-block / extra-block   a reference block with no counterpart in ours / ours with none in the reference\n"
    "  other             anything structural left\n"
    "\n"
    "Each finding prints the block offsets, a line of evidence and the source lever. The unit is built and compared\n"
    "with the configured backend (config/ctools.json); --batch takes every result that is not a MATCH, analyses the\n"
    "DIFF and SIZE ones whose wall (the structural class of unitcmp) is control-flow (--all-walls: every one;\n"
    "--stopped: only the functions parked with a stop line for that target) and writes batch.tsv, batch.json and\n"
    "batch.md to --out (default <build_dir>/cfg_diff). -v prints the block table, --dot / --html write\n"
    "<out>/<name>_<target>.dot / .html (the .html embeds an SVG when graphviz `dot` is on PATH).\n"
    "\n"
    "Exit code: 0 when every selected result is a MATCH, 1 when one is not, 2 for a usage or configuration error.\n"
    ""
